.TH SYNADM-TUI 1 "September 2026" "synadm-tui 0.22" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
synadm-tui \- terminal user interface for Matrix Synapse administration with synadm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B synadm-tui
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B synadm-tui
is a keyboard-oriented terminal interface for the Matrix Synapse administration
tool
.BR synadm .
It provides guided dialogs for common user, room, moderation, registration and
maintenance workflows while still executing the underlying synadm commands.
.PP
The interface includes a local demo backend for development and demonstrations
without a reachable Synapse server.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-synadm " " \fIPATH\fR
Use an alternative synadm executable. The default is
.BR synadm .
.TP
.B \-\-config-file " " \fIPATH\fR
Pass an alternative synadm configuration file to synadm.
.TP
.B \-\-timeout " " \fISECONDS\fR
Set the timeout for each synadm call. The default is 60 seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Start with the local demo backend instead of a real synadm connection.
.TP
.B \-\-demo-state " " \fIPATH\fR
Use a custom JSON file for the local demo backend state.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the program version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command line help and exit.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Up/Down, j/k
Move within the active column.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the selected area or execute the selected action.
.TP
.B Left, Esc, h
Return from the command column to the area column.
.TP
.B d
Toggle the local demo backend while the program is running.
.TP
.B c
Open the guided synadm configuration assistant.
.TP
.B t
Open the theme selector.
.TP
.B n
Open the single user creation assistant.
.TP
.B i
Open the CSV user import assistant.
.TP
.B /
Open user search.
.TP
.B x
Open the GDPR user deletion action.
.TP
.B a
Open the room creation assistant.
.TP
.B f
Open the global command palette.
.TP
.B ?
Show keyboard help.
.TP
.B q
Quit the program.
.SH DEMO MODE
The demo mode stores users, rooms and registration tokens in a local JSON file
and never contacts a Synapse server. By default the state file is:
.PP
.I ~/.local/state/synadm-tui/demo-server.json
.PP
Demo mode can be enabled at startup with
.B \-\-demo
or toggled at runtime with
.BR d .
When demo mode is active, the header contains
.BR "// D E M O" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/synadm-tui/
Theme settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/synadm-tui/audit.jsonl
Local audit log with redacted secrets.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/synadm-tui/demo-server.json
Default local demo backend state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR synadm (1)
.SH AUTHOR
synadm-tui contributors
